---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import site from '../config/site';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`How ${site.name} collects, uses and protects your information. We do not sell or share your personal information with lead brokers or third-party marketers.`}
  path="/privacy/"
  h1="Privacy Policy"
  lede="Short version: we collect what you send us, we use it to help you with Medicare, and we do not sell it to anybody."
  updated="August 2, 2026"
>
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {site.name} is an independent insurance agency operated by {site.agent.name}, National
    Producer Number {site.agent.npn}, based in {site.address.display}. You can reach us at
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or
    <a href={site.phone.href}>{site.phone.display}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>We only collect information you choose to give us. In practice that means:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Contact details you submit.</strong> Your name, phone number, email address and ZIP
      code when you fill in a form or call us.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>What you tell us about your situation.</strong> Your Medicare status, the doctors you
      want to keep, your prescriptions, and anything else you share so we can do useful work.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Basic technical information.</strong> Standard web server logs — IP address, browser
      type, pages requested — generated automatically when any browser loads any website.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>What our tools do not collect</h3>
  <p>
    The free tools on this site — the plan type finder, enrollment window checker, cost estimator
    and IRMAA estimator — run entirely in your browser. Nothing you type into them is transmitted
    to us or to anybody else, and nothing is stored on a server. Your date of birth, your income
    and your medication figures never leave your device.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where a tool remembers your answers between pages, it uses your browser's own session storage,
    which your browser clears when you close the tab.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <p>We use what you give us to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Respond to your inquiry and answer your questions</li>
    <li>Compare Medicare plans against your doctors, prescriptions and ZIP code</li>
    <li>Complete an enrollment application if you decide to enroll</li>
    <li>Service your coverage afterwards — billing questions, network changes, annual reviews</li>
    <li>Meet the record-keeping obligations that apply to licensed insurance agents</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we do not do</h2>
  <p>This is the part that matters most, so it is stated plainly:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>We do not sell your information.</strong> Not to lead brokers, not to marketing
      companies, not to anybody.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>We do not share it with other agents or agencies</strong> for their own marketing.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>We do not add you to unrelated mailing lists</strong> because you asked one Medicare
      question.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>We do not use advertising or cross-site tracking pixels</strong> on this website.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who we do share it with</h2>
  <p>Only where it is necessary to do the thing you asked for:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Insurance carriers</strong>, when you apply for a plan. An application cannot be
      submitted without it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Service providers</strong> who operate our email and customer records systems on our
      behalf, under confidentiality obligations.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Regulators or law enforcement</strong>, where we are legally required to.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Health information</h2>
  <p>
    Some of what you tell us — your medications, your conditions, your providers — is health
    information, and we treat it accordingly. It is used solely to compare plans and complete
    applications, shared only with the carriers required to process what you asked for, and never
    used for marketing.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact and consent</h2>
  <p>
    If you submit a form asking us to contact you, you are consenting to us reaching you at the
    number and email you provided, including by phone, text and email, about Medicare plan options.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Consent is not a condition of purchasing anything.</strong> Message and data rates may
    apply. Message frequency varies. You can opt out at any time — reply STOP to a text, reply HELP
    for help, click unsubscribe in an email, or just tell us, and we will stop.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>
      Mobile phone numbers and SMS consent collected on this site are never sold, rented or shared
      with third parties or affiliates for their own marketing purposes,
    </strong>
    and they are not shared with any other brand. We use them only to contact you about the request
    you made, and we share them only with the service providers that deliver those messages on our
    behalf.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This site sets no advertising or analytics cookies. Your browser may store small amounts of
    data locally so a tool can remember your answers as you move between pages; that data stays on
    your device and is cleared when you close the tab.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>You can, at any time:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Ask us what information we hold about you</li>
    <li>Ask us to correct anything that is wrong</li>
    <li>Ask us to delete your information, subject to the records we are legally required to keep</li>
    <li>Tell us to stop contacting you</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or call
    <a href={site.phone.href}>{site.phone.display}</a>. No form required.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This site is intended for adults considering Medicare coverage. We do not knowingly collect
    information from children.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes we will update the date at the top of the page. Material changes will be
    noted clearly rather than slipped in.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
